statement:
Let P, n ∈ ℕ, let U ⊆ ℝ^P, and let R = (C, θ, ξ), R₁ = (C₁, θ₁, ξ₁) and R₂ = (C₂, θ₂, ξ₂) be integer multiplicity triples in U (IMRep U n). Assume:
- C₁ ⊆ C and C₂ ⊆ C;
- ξ₁ = ξ and ξ₂ = ξ (as functions);
- θ(x) = 1_{C₁}(x)θ₁(x) + 1_{C₂}(x)θ₂(x) in ℕ for every x ∈ C.
Then the weight measures add: θHⁿ⌞C = θ₁Hⁿ⌞C₁ + θ₂Hⁿ⌞C₂, i.e. R.measure = R₁.measure + R₂.measure. The actions add: R.action ω = R₁.action ω + R₂.action ω for every ω ∈ 𝒟ⁿ(U).
